  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A velocity selector consists of electric field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> and magnetic field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mT</mi></math>. The value <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math>&nbsp;required for an electron of energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>728</mn><mi>eV</mi></math> moving along the positive <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>-axis to pass undeflected is&nbsp;</p><p>(Given, mass of electron <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>31</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>)</p>"
